From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:15:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple-vxd: Boot the firmware again after system sleep

The DEVA firmware boots on the first open and the driver then treats it
as running until it is unbound. System sleep turns the vdec domain off
whatever the runtime PM state, and the MTX loses the firmware with it.
After the first s2idle on an iPad 5 every decode failed:

  apple-vxd 207f00000.video-codec: TO_MTX indices out of range: rd 500361218 wr 3869108299 (capacity 390)
  apple-vxd 207f00000.video-codec: decode: push 1 of 1 failed: -5

and a hardware-decoded video played as a green picture until the driver
was bound again.

AppleD5500 starts the core again from the next submission:
submitCommandInternal (0xfffffff00628a8d4 in the iOS 16.7.10 J71t
kernelcache) powers an unpowered core up (PowerUpDeviceInternal,
0xfffffff00628baf8) and then loads and starts the firmware again
(0xfffffff00628d340, which clears 0x2014 and runs
LoadFirmwareAndStartCore) before it queues the command.

Do the same. On system suspend, stop taking jobs, let the one in flight
finish, and take the firmware down (rings, command buffers, image
buffer and the PM reference) as unbinding does; the loaded image is
kept. On resume, enable the core again, since runtime PM still counts
it active and its resume callback does not run, and take jobs again.
The next job, or the next open, boots the firmware from the kept image.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 .../media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-core.c | 54 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c | 15 +++++-
 2 files changed, 63 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-core.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-core.c
index a9777b0fe..cf7d5c299 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-core.c
@@ -226,18 +226,20 @@ void apple_vxd_run_postamble(struct apple_vxd_ctx *ctx,
 		v4l2_ctrl_request_complete(src_req, &ctx->ctrl_hdl);
 }
 
-/* Runtime PM stubs: the genpd (ps_vdec) does all the work. */
-static int apple_vxd_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
+/* The domain is on again: enable the core before anything reads it. */
+static void apple_vxd_integ_enable(struct apple_vxd_dev *vxd)
 {
-	struct apple_vxd_dev *vxd = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-
-	/* The domain is on again: enable the core before anything reads it. */
 	if (vxd->integ) {
 		writel(readl(vxd->integ + VXD_INTEG_CTRL) | VXD_INTEG_CTRL_ENABLE,
 		       vxd->integ + VXD_INTEG_CTRL);
 		udelay(VXD_INTEG_ENABLE_DELAY_US);
 	}
+}
 
+/* Runtime PM stubs: the genpd (ps_vdec) does all the work. */
+static int apple_vxd_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	apple_vxd_integ_enable(dev_get_drvdata(dev));
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -246,7 +248,49 @@ static int apple_vxd_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * System sleep turns the vdec domain off whatever the runtime PM state, and
+ * the MTX loses the firmware with it: after a wake every message went to
+ * rings that no longer existed ("TO_MTX indices out of range") and every
+ * decode failed.  AppleD5500 starts the core again from the next
+ * submission: submitCommandInternal (0xfffffff00628a8d4) powers an
+ * unpowered core up (PowerUpDeviceInternal, 0xfffffff00628baf8) and loads
+ * and starts the firmware again (0xfffffff00628d340) before it queues the
+ * command.  Do the same: stop taking jobs, let the one in flight finish,
+ * and take the firmware down with the domain; the next job (or open) boots
+ * it from the kept image.
+ */
+static int apple_vxd_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct apple_vxd_dev *vxd = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (vxd->m2m_dev)
+		v4l2_m2m_suspend(vxd->m2m_dev);
+	/* The watchdog finishes a job that never completes, so it goes last. */
+	flush_work(&vxd->job_done_work);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&vxd->watchdog_work);
+	apple_vxd_fw_cleanup(vxd);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int apple_vxd_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct apple_vxd_dev *vxd = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	/*
+	 * Runtime PM still counts the device active across the sleep, so its
+	 * resume callback does not run: the domain came back on without the
+	 * core enabled.
+	 */
+	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(dev))
+		apple_vxd_integ_enable(vxd);
+	if (vxd->m2m_dev)
+		v4l2_m2m_resume(vxd->m2m_dev);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct dev_pm_ops apple_vxd_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(apple_vxd_suspend, apple_vxd_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(apple_vxd_runtime_suspend, apple_vxd_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c
index 1d69d70bf..f862baa09 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c
@@ -784,6 +784,17 @@ static void apple_vxd_device_run(void *priv)
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A system sleep took the firmware down with the domain: start it
+	 * again before the job, as AppleD5500's submitCommandInternal does.
+	 * Once it runs this returns at once.
+	 */
+	ret = apple_vxd_boot_firmware(vxd);
+	if (ret) {
+		apple_vxd_job_finish(ctx, VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	ret = desc->ops->run(ctx);
 	if (ret)
 		apple_vxd_job_finish(ctx, VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
@@ -895,7 +906,9 @@ static int apple_vxd_open(struct file *filp)
 	/*
 	 * The DEVA firmware boots on the first open, from the image loaded
 	 * before this node was registered, and keeps running (and the block
-	 * powered) until the driver is unbound. Later opens find it running.
+	 * powered) until the driver is unbound or the system sleeps. Later
+	 * opens find it running; after a sleep, the next open or job boots it
+	 * again.
 	 */
 	ret = apple_vxd_boot_firmware(vxd);
 	if (ret)
-- 
2.49.0

